<title>USA: Brent crude inches up in U.S. aftermarket.</title>
<headline>Brent crude inches up in U.S. aftermarket.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>North Sea Brent crude oil inched up in the U.S. aftermarket on Tuesday in light activity, traders said.</p>
<p>A full boat of September Brent changed hands at $19.57 a barrel, up three cents from the IPE close.</p>
<p>Partial cargoes traded at $19.60 and $19.54, one a cash deal and one an exchange-for-physical transaction.</p>
<p>No intermonth spreads traded.</p>
<p>--Patricia Garip-Bertuol NY Energy Desk ((+1 212 859 1620))</p>
</text>
